{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-129925","model_call":25,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":12240,"output_tokens":232,"total_tokens":12472,"cached_tokens":11520,"reasoning_tokens":34},"output_characters":881,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_378001354#7_784192484","relevance":3,"reason":"This UK Essays document is dedicated to the impact of Gaius Marius' reforms and directly states several changes: eliminating the land requirement for army service, opening the military to any Roman male citizen including plebeians, improving training, replacing old soldier classes with cohorts, standardizing weapons, and professionalizing Rome's military.","learned":"Marius eliminated wealth/property-based recruitment limits, opened the army to poorer citizens, reorganized soldiers into cohorts, standardized legion equipment/symbols, and professionalized the Roman military."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1869","reason":"The legions/cohorts query is producing direct evidence about another major aspect of Marius' change; continue to find more grade-3 documents or segments."}}}
