{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-129925","model_call":27,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ marius capite censi army reforms)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ marius capite censi army reforms)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_378001354#8_784194451","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1871","rank":1,"snippet":"2019). This opportunity opened the military to any Roman male citizen, including the Plebeian classes. Marius improved Roman military training by using various techniques developed by ancient gladiators. These military reforms also replaced the original three soldier classes to many cohorts of men who were all armed with a gladius (short sword) and used the eagle to formalise the standard of all legions in the army. Marius’s motivations behind the reforms did exactly what was wished, to professionalise and revolutionise Rome’s military (Matthew, 2006). Marius’ military reforms relied on removing the land requirements needed to join the Roman <cover>army. This reform allowed Marius access to the largest class of population in Rome, the Capite Censi. Past Roman reforms </cover>only allowed the Capite Censi to join the military only if Rome were facing military emergencies. ( Nofi, 2019). The benefit of allowing the Capite Censi to join the Roman army was the expansion of the Roman military.\" , \"start_char\": 5403.000000 , \"title\": \"Impact of Gaius Marius’ Reforms\" , \"url\": \"https://www.ukessays.com/essays/history/impact-of-gaius-marius-reforms.php\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_378001354#8_784194451","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":43},"model_calls":27,"document_judgments":22,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
