{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-129925","model_call":27,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1871"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1871"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_378001354#9_784196069","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1871","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_378001354#9_784196069\" , \"end_char\": 7422.000000 , \"headings\": \"Impact of Gaius Marius’ Reforms Impact of Gaius Marius’ Reforms Get Help With Your Essay Rationale: Interest: Inquiry: Choice: Sources: Cite This Work DMCA / Removal Request \" , \"segment\": \"Marius’ military reforms relied on removing the land requirements needed to join the Roman <cover>army. This reform allowed Marius access to the largest class of population in Rome, the Capite Censi. Past Roman reforms </cover>only allowed the Capite Censi to join the military only if Rome were facing military emergencies. ( Nofi, 2019). The benefit of allowing the Capite Censi to join the Roman army was the expansion of the Roman military. Consequently, the landless troops who had nowhere to live after serving posed a dangerous precedent for the Roman hierarchy as senators had to offer retirement benefits like grants of land from newly conquered areas (White, 2011). After these reforms were introduced, the Germanic and Celtic tribes were crushed by the revolutionised Roman army. Marius fought for his soldier’s rights and persuaded the Senate to ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_378001354#9_784196069","rank":2,"relevance":3}]},"time":6},"model_calls":27,"document_judgments":22,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
