{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-129925","model_call":46,"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_1567251276#7_3198736906"},"record":{"query":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_1567251276#7_3198736906","op":"document"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_1567251276#7_3198736906","document":"What were the impact of the military reforms of Marius on Rome? - DailyHistory.org ... What were the impact of the military reforms of Marius on Rome? What were the impact of the military reforms of Marius on Rome? Background The career of Marius Marius Reforms The social and political impact of the Marian Reforms Impact on the military Conclusion References  ... It appears that the Scipio family acted as the patrons of the young Marius and this greatly helped his career. Marius later married Julia, the aunt of Julius Caesar. He then served as an officer in Rome’s war with the North African king Jurgutha. This war was to make the reputation of Marius as a soldier and a general. Marius was eventually given command of the army in the war against Jurgutha, and he proved to be a charismatic leader with real military talent. He developed a new strategy to deal with the king and soon captured him. During his time in North Africa, he began the first of his military reforms, which were technically illegal. Marius was very concerned with citizens' reluctance to enroll in the army and the declining number of recruits available to Rome. Marius was later elected one of Rome’s two consuls, and he was elected to that office an unprecedented seven times. He was associated with the Populares, and his policies were often informed by the need to help the urban and the rural poor.","ok":true,"op":"document"},"time":21},"model_calls":46,"document_judgments":36,"relevance_3":11,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
